  "planning_notes": [
    "IR proximity sensor on D2 is modeled as a digital input; polarity/active level is not specified, so catalog default is used (digital_input active_high default).",
    "Water-level decision thresholds (distance-to-percentage mapping, low-level cutoff) are business-model parameters not provided in the prompt; outputs/validity provide raw cm and validity only.",
    "Ultrasonic timeout_us is set to 30000 within the supported 25000..60000 range; sample_period_ms alignment to control_period_ms and response budget must be handled in SysML.",
    "TM1637 is driven by a single tm1637_number port on CLK=D4, DIO=D5. The prompt requires displaying remaining water percentage and today's usage count, but exact multiplexing/encoding rules (e.g., when to show percent vs count, formatting/blanking) are not specified; those rules belong in the model.",
    "Serial query protocol (which commands trigger the report, exact frame handling) is not fully specified; framing is assumed line_or_idle at 9600 baud per the provided serial settings. Report gate is modeled as a boolean trigger set by SysML upon a successful query."
  ],
